Since p(S1)comb1 > p(S1)comb2, the dierence p(S1)comb1 − p(S1)comb2 is always positive.
Subsequently, the requisite p(F1|S1) > p(F1|S2) results to be a necessary and sucient condition which veries p(F1)comb1 > p(F1)comb2. Clearly the values of p(F1|S1) and p(F1|S2)
are unknown so that, in order to verify the condition, an estimate of these probabilities is
required.
Extending the same procedure to all the possible combinations, similar conditions are ob127

tained:
