Let Y = {YCh, YNCh}, where YCh includes all the discrete nodes having at least one continuous
parent in the initial eBN (YCh = {Y ∩ [ch(X1) ∪ ch(X2) ∪ ... ∪ ch(Xm)} where ch(Xi)
is the set of children nodes of a generic node Xi) and YNCh all the discrete nodes of the eBN with
only discrete parents. Since the aim of the methodology is to eliminate the continuous variables in
the network only these latter and their children nodes will be subject to changes in the reduction
procedure: the elimination of continuous nodes will affect directly the parents of the nodes in
YCh and hence their CPTs. On the contrary, the nodes in YNCh will stay unchanged and keep
the same parents and CDTs in the eBN as in the rBN (pa(Y(j)) = pa0(Y(j)), ∀Y(j) ∈ YNCh,
where pa0
(Y(j)) refers to the parents of the generic node Y(j) in the rBN). Hence, Eq.A.5, can be
rewritten as:
P(Y) = ΠYi∈YCh p[yi|pa(Yi)] Z
