Since these latter, thanks to the integration, do not include any reference to continuous variables,
the continuous nodes and their related links can be removed from the initial model obtaining the
final reduced network rBN. As already mentioned, the main advantage of this approach is that
the information initially stored in the continuous variables is not empoverished or lost but just
processed and reformulated in the form of conditional probabilities associated with the nodes in
YCh.
